Dashboard widget listing local devices by traffic, split into download and
upload. Historical ranges come from the built-in NetFlow/Insight aggregator;
a Live view streams current rates, updated every second, from the pf state
table. No extra collector is required.

Pick a range (live, last hour, last 24 hours, today, yesterday, last 7 days
or a custom range) and a scope (all traffic, or internet only). Filter by
network, hostname or IP, sort any column, and click a device for its top
peers and ports. Totals can be charted as a pie or a stacked bar.

Local networks and the upstream interface come from the firewall's own
interfaces (and, for Live, its routes), and hostnames from Dnsmasq DHCP
leases and host records. Nothing is hardcoded.

WWW: https://github.com/nycoagung/opnsense-plugin-topdevices

Plugin Changelog
----------------

0.3.0

* Yesterday runs from 00:00:00 to 23:59:59, exactly, in both scopes: the
  plugin keeps NetFlow's raw flow log for two days (hard links to the files
  core rotates out, about 250 MB here), and ranges starting within the last
  50 hours are read from it
* Midnights, the custom range fields and every caption follow the time zone
  set under System: Settings: General, not the browser's (which is used only
  when the firewall does not say)
* Internet only for Today and Last 24 hours no longer falls short late in the
  evening, when the day outgrew core's own log
* A range reaching back before NetFlow began collecting starts its caption
  at the oldest bucket NetFlow returned, and says so

0.2.0

* Last hour, Today, Last 24 hours and custom ranges starting within the last
  day are exact to the second in both scopes: read on demand from NetFlow's
  raw flow log (about a day of flows), with no cron job and no database
* Where a range reaches past the log, all traffic is filled in from NetFlow's
  hourly records, and internet only says how much it covers
* The device panel's peers and ports cover exactly the table's window
* The privilege is now called "Dashboard: Top Devices"; it also needs
  "Diagnostics: Network Insight" to read the new endpoints

0.1.2

* Fixed: the NetFlow ranges read whole UTC days, so Last hour showed
  everything since 10:00 (UTC+10), Last 24 hours and Today both everything
  since 10:00 the day before, and Yesterday two days
* All traffic reads 5-minute buckets for Last hour and hourly ones for Last
  24 hours and Today; every window snaps to whole buckets
* The caption shows the span the figures cover, with a note when daily
  buckets stand in for a shorter range (internet only, older history)
* Ranges further back than NetFlow keeps (62 days for internet only and the
  drill-down, a year for all traffic) are cut to what is kept, and say so
* Switching scope while data loads can no longer show one scope's rows under
  the other's caption; switching back reuses the loaded data
* Yesterday follows the calendar across daylight-saving changes

0.1.1

* Live: a tab shown again reconnects at once, even after three failed
  connects while it was hidden
* Sampler: a failed WAN counter read no longer discards that sample's device
  rates, and command output that is not UTF-8 no longer fails a read
* Installer: a failed download no longer leaves /tmp/tdinst.* behind
* Names are escaped inside quoted attributes as well

0.1.0

* Live view: per-device download and upload rates, streamed from the pf
  state table and updated every second
* Live: pick which devices to watch, so the table keeps its size and order;
  no column sorting in Live
* Live: a line graph of each device's download over the last minute; a y-axis
  that holds its highest value; with nothing picked, a fixed row count where
  only the busiest device moves
* The live sampler throttles itself, checks its totals against the WAN
  counters and restarts hourly
* The installer adds the live backend, clears the ACL cache and restarts
  configd detached

0.0.1

* Initial release
